From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:56:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 176/177] feat(gastown): ship the polecat submit push-gate and
 reassign fences as a pack executable (gcp-nc8wg)

submit-and-exit cost ~13.4K output tokens and 8.3 calls per bead because the model retyped the 302-line push-gate fence and the 64-line reassign fence at the end of every bead, for a step that is entirely deterministic.

Both fences now live in gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-submit.sh (modes push-gate and reassign), lifted verbatim between sentinels. Every formula substitution inside them became an explicit PS_* env var (PS_CONVOY_ID, PS_BASE_BRANCH, PS_BINDING_PREFIX); the script carries no {{. It derives WORK_BEAD_ID from the convoy with the same jq expression sections 0 and 1 use, and CURRENT_BRANCH from git. Each fence in mol-polecat-work.toml is now a 12-line stub using the v9mvh locator (gc formula list --json .source, dirname twice) and a single PS_<NAME>=... bash "$PS" <mode> call. The not-found path does the guarded own-step close before drain-ack, so the drain-ack-closes-own-step contract still holds. The step text drops from 689 to 391 lines.

Intentional behaviour additions, all fail-safe: a missing script stops with submit_script_missing; a convoy without exactly one child stops with exit 1 before any write; target is now quoted.

The tests that pinned text in the old fences are re-pointed to the script in the same change (test_polecat_push_gate, test_polecat_handoff_stamp, test_gastown_pack_assets, test_refinery_find_work, the inference gate and its test, test_v2_drain_ack_closes_own_step), and test_polecat_submit.sh adds the behavioural cases. The stale test comment claiming every submit block re-derives its ids now says what is true.

Applied verbatim from the seat-verified artifact in gcp-dy5es (sha256 2d2f6859). Validation: see the acceptance notes on gcp-nc8wg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
